# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 2.6200e+03 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 1.4760 79.820 8.9097e+04 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~80 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 5.2830 28.363 1.1291e+08 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 4 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 - drag_overtakes_ablation 5.2835 28.326 1.1320e+08 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
5 F flare 5.2892 28.259 2.9367e+08 stylized  Light rises x3.8 in 0.10 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 28.3 km (82% of m0); split gen 0 at 28.2 km (81% of m0). Dust groups supply 37% of the rise and 27% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
6 B first_breakup 5.2932 28.212 4.7875e+08 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x4.2 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
7 P peak 5.2962 28.200 5.4360e+08 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+1.0 km from the peak of energy deposition (27.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 12.9 km/s).
8 D rolloff 5.4642 26.325 1.9888e+08 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.17 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 74% of v0, 62% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
9 T tail 6.2772 21.155 5.3985e+05 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
10 R retirement_step 6.3072 21.047 3.9255e+05 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 29% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
